{ Exercise. Try the questions in the book before reading this line. } 1. Rxe1 Rxe1+ 2. Bf1 { Illustrative line. Black has another rook on e8. The e-file between the two black rooks is clear, so it can replace the rook that White captures. Rxe1 Rxe1+ leaves White facing a second rook check. Ending the calculation after White's first capture would miss this reply. Bf1 blocks the line using the diagonal c4-d3-e2-f1. The white king on g1 protects f1; if Black plays ...Rxf1+, Kxf1 takes that last rook. White has found a continuing defense, not merely one legal move. The sample does not attempt to solve the entire resulting endgame. } *

[Event "Find a Defensive Resource / 07.2A"]
