{ Making an escape square can prevent back-rank mate. The square must be empty, reachable by the king, and free of enemy attacks after the check arrives. } 1. h3 Re1+ 2. Kh2 { Illustrative line. h3 creates an escape square. If Black plays ...Re1+, Kh2 steps off the first rank. The rook on e1 attacks f1 and h1, but it does not attack h2. This is one preventive choice, not the only move. White could also investigate a king move or other pawn moves. The point is to test the intended escape after the opponent's check, when the board has actually changed. } *

