{ Exercise. Try the questions in the book before reading this line. } 1. Nxh4 { Illustrative line. The knight has moved from f2 to f3. From f3 it attacks h4, the square occupied by Black's queen. This one-square change creates a much stronger resource. Nxh4 captures the queen. No black piece can recapture the knight on h4 immediately. White should notice this before considering a queen exchange or a pawn move. A forcing capture can eliminate the threat and gain decisive material. Qxd6 remains a way to remove the bishop, but taking the queen is the larger opportunity. Defensive thinking should begin with the actual legal captures, not with an assumption that only passive moves are available. } *
